WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.201
-Here's how this works.

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.770
In front of us are two envelopes
containing confessions.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.472
One is true.
The other is a lie.

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:07.773
Once you read the confession,

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.608
the other two players
get to interrogate you.

00:00:09.608 --> 00:00:11.844
Then they have to come to
a unanimous decision --

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.546
is it the truth
or is it a lie?

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.481
-Bring it on!
-Alright.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.016
Ryan, you'll go first.
-I go first.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:18.518
Oh, I'm so excited, you guys.
-Which one?

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.419
-I'm going with --
I'm going with number 1.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:21.420
-Okay.
-Right?

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.422
-Nice.
-I suppose. Yeah, sure.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.490
-I think that's a good idea.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.925
-This might be part of
the ruse already.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:31.564
-"My mom once washed her hands
with a urinal cake."

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.433
-What's a urinal cake?
-Good question.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.269
-Alright.
-I'm glad you asked me that.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:38.705
-It's at the bottom of a urinal

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:39.706
when you go into the men's room.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.740
-I don't visit those very often.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.241
-It looks like
a little white puck.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:43.610
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.845
-It might be confused with soap.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.047
-Wait. But where was your mom
when this happened?

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:50.783
-She was at a funeral.
True story.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:55.120
-How long ago was this?
-This was about two months ago.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.589
-What?!
-Yep.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.891
-Wait. Wait. So, your mom --

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.360
Your mom did what
with a urinal cake?

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.794
-It was an outdoor funeral.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:03.796
There was, like, a little sort
of porta-potty-type thing

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.732
that had both the --
you know, the toilet,

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.768
and then it also had, like,
this little space-aged

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.071
kind of urinal thing that could
very easily be confused

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.738
as a sink with a little
puck in it.

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:14.974
Alright, it was me, not my mom!

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.675
No. No, no.
It was my mom.

00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:19.879
And she accidentally used
the urinal cake,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.181
thinking it was soap,
washing her hands.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:24.083
-The urinal cake was up
by the sink?

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.184
-No, it was right in
this sort of

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.086
space-aged little urinal thing.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.320
-In what city was this
porta-potty in?

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.889
-This was in -- just outside of

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.057
Vancouver, British Columbia,
Canada.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.525
-Alright then.
Anything happens in Canada.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.859
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Alright.

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:36.095
-She washed her hands with it
and then left going like,

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.497
"Ooh, it smells funny.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.198
This urinal cake is very --"

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:42.368
-Did she flush, like, thinking
that was the faucet

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.070
and just --
with the urine water?

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.271
-That I do not know, Jimmy.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.940
-Alright, I'm going to say
I don't know.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:47.940
I don't know.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.142
-I'm gonna say --

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.443
-If it did happen,
it's really funny,

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.645
but I don't think
it really happened.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.281
-I'm going to say
that it's a lie,

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.682
because there's -- I don't know.

00:01:56.682 --> 00:02:00.019
There's just some hesitation in
the facial expressions.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.788
-I'm going to say it's a lie,
because I think if you went

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:05.391
to a funeral outdoors, I've
never seen a porta-potty

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.759
by the cemetery.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.360
-Gotta go, you gotta go.
-By the cemetery?

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.797
Well, I mean, someone did go,
I guess, right?

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.131
-Yeah.
-True or lie?

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:13.366
-This is true.
-What?!

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:16.936
-Oh, my God! What?!
-True.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.005
-Your mom did that?
-Oh, my God!

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.907
-In her defense,
a lot of people don't know

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.309
that that's a urinal cake.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.544
-I didn't know what
a urinal cake was.

00:02:25.544 --> 00:02:27.012
I actually would have made
the same mistake.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:29.649
-Also, like, what kind of A-hole
calls it a cake?

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:30.883
-Yeah.
-Like, right?

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:34.420
-It sounds so pleasant.
-Alright. Here we go.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.955
It's my turn. Here we go.
Alright.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.990
Which envelope should I open?
1 or 2?

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:38.992
-2.
-I say 2.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.392
-Let's mix it up.
-Yeah, 2.

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:41.861
-Why not?
-Here we go.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.430
-Yes.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.533
-"There is a bronze statue of me
at the bottom of the lake

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.902
next to Neil Young's farmhouse."

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:53.907
-What? That is so specific.
When was the statue made?

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.509
-The statue was made in
the early 2000s.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.044
I'll tell you exactly what --
It was an award or something

00:02:59.044 --> 00:03:02.348
that was actually given to me by
Regis and Kelly Ripa.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.050
-Kelly?
-Back when Regis was on.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.851
-Okay. Not Kathie Lee.
This is the Kelly era.

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:07.620
-No, this is "Relly."
-Wow. Okay.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.555
-This is Regis and Kelly.
-What's the -- Sorry.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.023
-They gave me an award,
like, some Jimmy Fallon award.

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:12.224
I did their show.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:14.394
-And then they promptly
threw it in a lake.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.696
-No. What happened was,
I was flying to Neil's,

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.964
'cause I was doing his
Bridge School benefit,

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:19.999
which is a great charity.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.400
-Yep.
-And I was going with Lorne.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.501
And we were going right --

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.737
I went right after I did
"Regis and Kelly,"

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.138
so I had my --
Everything was packed.

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:29.909
I had an actual statue of me
that they gave me, on the plane.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.378
So when I landed,
I had this statue of me.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.545
And it was just --
I thought it would be funny

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:34.580
to show it to people.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.915
-And how did it end up
in a lake?

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:36.949
-Because everyone was
making fun of me

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:38.251
that I had a statue of myself.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.119
-So you threw it in a lake,

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.654
like the Heart of the Ocean
in "Titanic."

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.155
You just let it go.
-Yes. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:44.657
"My Heart Will Go On."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:48.627
-I had a few...beverages, and
everyone was passing it around,

00:03:48.627 --> 00:03:50.429
accepting the award
and all this bit.

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:53.799
-So, wait.
What was the size of the statue?

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:55.868
-And it was bronze.
-It was bronzed.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.637
It was, like,
aluminum foil on plastic.

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:00.239
-It's next to a statue of

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:01.307
Neil Young at
Neil Young's farmhouse?

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.875
-No, I was at Neil Young's
farmhouse,

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.176
and I threw it in the lake.

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:05.545
-Is Neil Young aware of this?
-Yeah, he was there.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:06.846
-He's there?

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.148
-I'm going to say -- This
actually sounds true to me.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.583
It doesn't sound too crazy.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.717
-I'm gonna go with --
Camila's right.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.619
-Okay, okay, okay.
-True. Okay, let's do it.

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.054
-It never happened.
I made it up.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:18.991
-Oh! I was there!
-Wait.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.993
-I made it up. I know.
-Oh!

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:23.095
-I've never been
to Neil Young's house.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.598
That is the best acting of --
You've seen my movies.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.033
You've seen my movies, right?

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.801
I mean, this is the best acting
I've ever done.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.504
-Yeah, what are you doing?
I'm terrified of you.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.272
-Camila, I love you.
It's your turn to go.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.808
-Alright.
-I think number 1, right?

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.543
-I think number 1 for sure.
-Number 1. Alright. Okay.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.380
Let's see.
-Let's see. Alrighty.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.917
-I once lost -- this is your
friend -- Taylor Swift's cat.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.786
-You once lost her cat?
-You lost her cat?

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.287
-I lost her cat.
-This is a big deal.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:49.288
-Would you like to hear
the story?

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:50.356
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.325
-So, we were on
tour together last year.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.859
I was opening for her
on her Reputation Stadium Tour.

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:55.160
-Mm-hmm.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.097
-And she basically --
She asked me to babysit her cat.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.965
Her cat kind of had, like,
a weird little

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:01.300
stomach-infection thing.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.668
She was gonna go do
a meet and greet.

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:04.003
We were hanging out
in the dressing room.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.972
I'm taking care of her cat.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.006
Somebody from my team asked
me to do something.

00:05:08.006 --> 00:05:09.842
I leave the door open.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:13.446
The cat, Meredith, sneaks out,
is nowhere to be found.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.646
-Yeah.

00:05:14.646 --> 00:05:17.583
-Hours pass,
and nobody can find the cat.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.652
-Yeah.
-Where are you? What city?

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.987
-It was also
in Vancouver, actually.

00:05:21.987 --> 00:05:24.590
-This is already reeking like
a whole lot of bull.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.860
-No, no, no.
It was in Vancouver.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.294
-Oh, really?
-Ask me more questions.

00:05:29.294 --> 00:05:30.896
-Yeah, yeah. Meredith.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:32.498
I love that you threw in
the name Meredith.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:36.769
-Everybody knows that cats are
banned in Vancouver.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:37.903
-That's not true.

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.705
-Wait. So, wait.
So, the cat's sick.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:41.474
That's when she asked you
to babysit the cat?

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.442
-Well, it's not like she was
like, "Please babysit the cat."

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:46.245
I was already hanging out with
her in the dressing room.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:49.415
-And what was the cat like?
The cat's sick.

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.549
Is it moving around
or is it laying there?

00:05:50.549 --> 00:05:52.284
-And she was like,
"Take my cat with this

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:55.054
unpredictable stomach issue
and enjoy it for a while."

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.088
No. Really?

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:58.357
-No, I mean, the cat was --
You know,

00:05:58.357 --> 00:05:59.891
answering your question about
the cat's activity,

00:05:59.891 --> 00:06:01.327
it was just laying there.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:04.463
That's why I did not expect for
the cat to leave the door.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:07.133
-So, you're saying that someone
removed the cat from the --

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.201
-No. I'm saying I left
the door open.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:10.636
I didn't think the cat
was going to go anywhere.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.504
-Camila, don't give me this.
This is ridiculous.

00:06:12.504 --> 00:06:16.776
I mean, now, who found the cat?
Who found the cat?

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:18.177
-One of her security guards.
It was literally --

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:19.212
-Which one?

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:20.279
I know all of her
security guards.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:22.248
-Yeah. Was it Dan?
-No, was it Steve?

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:24.884
-Was it Gil?
-I don't know his name!

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:28.087
She has 13!
-A lot of holes in this story.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:30.556
-Okay. And then the cat
was found in, like, one of

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:31.724
the seats of the golf cart.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:33.426
I don't know the security
guard's name, okay?

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:35.561
I'm sorry. There's a lot.
-Is this true?

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:36.562
I think this is true.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:37.730
-I feel like it's true.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.098
-Yeah, I think we broke her,
'cause she was --

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:40.099
-I know.

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:41.167
-I think what happened was --

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.234
we were being fooled
the whole time.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.535
We were being played.

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:45.270
-She's also one question away
flipping the table.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.139
-Yeah, that's true.
-You better say it's true.

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:50.642
-I'm gonna say true.
-True. Yes.

00:06:50.642 --> 00:06:52.178
-This is false!
-What?!

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:56.615
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:58.350
-Really?!
-How did you do that?

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.219
-No, no, no. Wait, wait, wait.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:01.721
Did you actually
think it was true --

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:02.855
-Yeah. 100%.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.856
-Because I feel like I'm a
terrible --

00:07:04.856 --> 00:07:06.725
I came into this game
knowing I'm a bad liar.

00:07:06.725 --> 00:07:09.362
-It was the golf-cart thing.
-You have a black belt in lying.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.530
-Really?
-Yes.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.532
-That was pretty great.
-Yes! We're liars!

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:15.000
We're good liars!
-Wait, don't do that.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.802
You guys are the greatest.
-Amazing.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:19.872
-Our thanks to Ryan Reynolds,
Camila Cabello.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.040
That was good.

